00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:52.023
- [Host] I can't be honest about who I am.

00:10:53.035 --> 00:10:56.035
(suspenseful music)

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:00.120
- [Bob] When I was in middle school,

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:00.990
being Muslim,

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:03.810
I was really afraid to
tell people I was Muslim

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:06.870
because a lot of people
would make terrorist jokes

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:07.800
all the time.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.840
And I would get really embarrassed

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:10.797
when my mom would pick me up

00:11:10.797 --> 00:11:12.930
and my grandma, who wears a hijab,

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:15.090
would be sitting in the passenger seat.

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:16.927
And then everybody would
look at them and be like,

00:11:16.927 --> 00:11:17.970
"Oh, you're Muslim?"

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.280
I was just, it was, I can't
believe I thought that way.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.410
The things I would do to go back to that

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:23.460
and see my grandma again.

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:26.280
But sometimes I feel like

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.590
I wanna wear a head scarf outside

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:31.620
but I get scared that I'll be, like,

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.333
I'll get something thrown at me.

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:37.350
And I don't know, it's a fear of mine.

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:39.810
And I know a lot of people,
they don't experience that

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:42.360
but I also know some that do.

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:45.030
- [Alex] I've been battling
with mental illness,

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:47.520
I am diagnosed with OCD,

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:49.500
PTSD, anxiety.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:53.370
And I might get tested for
bipolar, being bipolar.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:55.980
You know, growing up, I
experienced two murders.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:57.510
I've experienced sexual assault.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:12:00.150
You know, I grew up in South Los Angeles,

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:01.530
which is a violent neighborhood.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.960
So I've seen a lot of dark shit.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.240
And you know, I was sexually assaulted

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:09.270
by my own uncle, like, and my family,

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.500
they're right now trying to

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.340
understand me,

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:16.743
but they were, you know, in denial.

00:12:18.262 --> 00:12:21.060
And a lot of my trauma
has really affected me.

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:23.250
I would say OCD really has affected me

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:25.980
because it affects my relationships.

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:27.870
Because a lot of people judge me

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.340
when I tell them I have OCD.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:32.970
And one major thing that people
don't understand about me

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:36.540
is I find it gross if you
had previous partners.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:39.150
And a lot of people think
it's 'cause I'm misogynistic.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:41.040
I don't know, what's the word.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:42.810
But it's not that.

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:45.120
I've talked to my psychiatrist about this.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:48.210
And she told me that it's
the fear of contamination.

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:50.910
I'm battling these inner, you know,

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:54.318
my disease or whatever you wanna call it.

00:12:54.318 --> 00:12:56.970
But it's tiring living with OCD

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:58.863
and it's just super damn hard.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.360
- [Valerie] Honestly, all of high school,

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:06.390
I have been happy with who I am.

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:07.800
I met my girlfriend.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:10.290
She also told me like,

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.390
after, like, I fell in love
with her and everything.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:16.980
Like, she told me that her
family is really homophobic.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:19.170
But then she breaks the news like,

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:22.470
oh, like they're homophobic
to the point where like,

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:26.040
I can't even like surround
myself with gay people.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.080
You know, I love my girlfriend so much

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:29.820
and I want to be around her.

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:32.820
I literally had to go back

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:34.230
into the closet.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:36.000
That's like a really big shift for me

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.430
because I'm out, like, in seventh grade.

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:42.030
And then senior year of high
school, I'm shoved back in.

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:45.360
And I know I should, like,
remove myself from this

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.880
but I really can't because

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:50.910
I'm dating her and not her family.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:53.100
It just like sucks hearing, like,

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:54.990
all that, like, stuff,

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:56.910
especially 'cause my brother's trans

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.700
and all of like my siblings

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.820
are literally part of the LGBTQ community.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:05.220
I know the easiest way is
to like break up with her.

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:07.140
But like she did nothing wrong.

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:08.523
Like she's,

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:14.310
she's unlearning
everything they taught her.

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:15.930
I even went to her church

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:18.420
and they talk about gay people too.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:19.620
And it's just sad.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:23.070
And like, I just think of
her going through it alone.

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.530
And like, she has to hear that too.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:27.570
Like, it's not just me taking the hit,

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:28.893
it's also her.

00:14:30.327 --> 00:14:32.230
(sniffles) I'm sorry.
- No, I'm sorry.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.490
- [Bob] I love talking
about different issues,

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:38.250
especially since we're all
like around the same age,

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:39.083
I thought it was really cool.

00:14:39.083 --> 00:14:41.130
I've never got to experience
something like this.

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:42.090
- [Avery] I enjoyed it,

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:44.910
feeling like we could talk
about anything and everything

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:46.590
without fear of repercussion.

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:47.423
- [Jessica] I think it was good

00:14:47.423 --> 00:14:48.780
to hear everyone else's opinions

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:52.020
to realize that we're not as
different as we think we are.

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:53.130
We have a lot in common

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:54.420
and I think that's really comforting.

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:56.010
So I'm really glad to learn

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:58.838
that people have the same ideas as me.

00:14:58.838 --> 00:15:01.921
(upbeat tense music)

